\description{
Labels a clustering's cells from a labeled single-cell reference, as a job, in the Cell types view: an AnnData object in Zarr (a folder or a zip; its cells' labels in an obs column, its counts or log-normalized values in X, raw/X or a layer), or a table of each label's mean expression (CSV, TSV or Parquet; a row per label or per gene). The reference is restricted to the panel's genes; each label's profile is its cells' mean log-normalized expression; each cell is correlated (Spearman) with each label's profile over the genes most higher in one label than another, then again on the leading labels' own genes until one is left (Aran et al. 2019), and takes the last round's best when it leads the next by the margin. An .h5ad file is read once written as Zarr (anndata's write_zarr). The columns are found by their usual names unless given. Recorded as a labels artifact; asking again answers it. Answers the genes shared, the cells labeled, each label's cells and each cluster's leading labels.
}
\seealso{\code{\link{sc_call}}, which sends any action by its name (here \code{"reference_labels"}).}
